---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Stage 1 — Chain anchor DAG · enprot">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-3">Stage 1 — Chain anchor DAG</h1>
  <p class="text-enprot-muted mb-6">
    Tamper-evident, merge-friendly, capability-scoped history. The blockchain-in-a-file core.
  </p>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Goal</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">
      Every meaningful mutation produces a chain anchor that attests: "the file looked like this
      at this point, signed by me, building on these previous anchors." Anchors form a DAG, not a
      linear chain, so multiple writers can fork and merge without locks.
    </p>
    <p>
      See <a href="/docs/chain-dag" class="text-enprot-accent hover:underline">Chain DAG deep dive</a>
      for the full algorithm.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Demonstration: signed release notes</h2>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code># One-time setup: release officer's keypair
enprot keygen ed25519 --out-priv release.pem --out-pub release.pub

# Each release adds a signed anchor to release-notes.ept
enprot encrypt --anchor --signer release.pem \
    -w ReleaseNotes -k ReleaseNotes=$(date +%s) \
    release-notes.ept

# Anyone can verify the full history
enprot verify-chain --trust-root $(enprot fingerprint release.pub) \
    release-notes.ept</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
      The resulting file has chain anchors interleaved with the content, each committing to
      the file state at that point and signed by the release officer. Tampering with any
      past release breaks verification.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Demonstration: append-only audit log</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">
      A common special case: each line becomes its own anchor. See
      <a href="/docs/examples/audit-log" class="text-enprot-accent hover:underline">the audit log example</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Status</h2>
    <p>
      Specified in <a href="https://github.com/engyon/enprot/blob/main/TODO.finalize/17-chain-dag.md" class="text-enprot-accent hover:underline"><code>TODO.finalize/17</code></a>
      and <a href="https://github.com/engyon/enprot/blob/main/TODO.finalize/18-verify-chain.md" class="text-enprot-accent hover:underline"><code>TODO.finalize/18</code></a>.
      Implementation: <code>src/ledger/</code> module + new <code>CHAIN</code> directive + <code>verify-chain</code> subcommand.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
